This add-on assumes the METIS-5 package to be available and installed.

The METIS-5 package (metis5.1.0.tar.gz) can be obtained from:
      http://glaros.dtc.umn.edu/gkhome/metis/metis/download
However it is often down and we recommend to download metis5.1.0.tar.gz
from an alternative reliable source, such as
      https://github.com/mfem/tpls

Note: The GitHub repo 
      https://github.com/KarypisLab/METIS
contains a newer version of metis, but the API has been changed and a lot of
software, including MA57 and MUMPS, doesn't work anymore with this version 
of metis.

Note: The Fedora Linux distribution and macOS (via Homebrew) have precompiled
libs of metis5.1.0. See also the file install/INSTALL.fedora in the tfem root.

Note: the default install of METIS-5 generates a version for 32bit integers.
See the install instructions METIS-5 on how to build a version with 64bit
integers. 


Installation
============

- Use or install version 5.1.0 of METIS-5.

- build add-on using

     make metis5

- Adjust Mdefs.mk according to the directions given in the comments.

Usage
=====

Two distinct ways of using METIS are provided:

  1) Renumbering of the nodes of the mesh to minimize sparse matrix fill-in
  2) Renumbering of the degrees of freedom of the problem to minimize sparse
     matrix fill-in.

The first is the most easy one, but it does not take Lagrange multipliers,
additional unknowns, connections ... into account. The second is based on
the actual matrix structure and therefore is more general. The latter 
requires the matrix to be fully built, before it can be applied.

Ad 1 (renumbering nodes):
------------------------

A simple main program that renumbers the nodes using metis is given by:

  program myprog

  ...

  use metis5_m

  ...

  <create or read the mesh>

  call fill_mesh_parts ( mesh )

  call renumber_metis ( mesh )

  ...

  end program myprog

Remarks on renumbering nodes:

- The renumbered nodes are used in the numbering of the degrees of freedom
  for the system vector/matrix. For all other purposes the original numbering
  is used.

- The routines write_mesh/read_mesh read/write renumbering info. So it is not
  necessary to call renumber_metis for the mesh again after reading a mesh
  that has been renumbered before writing.

- The routine METIS_NodeND is used.

- For big 3D flow problems where the number of reals in the matrix and/or
  preconditioner exceeds 2^31, the size of mesh%nodnod is likely to be
  still well below 2^31 (for 3D flow problems the size of mesh%nodnod
  is usually one order lower than the number of reals in the matrix). For these
  cases MeTis-5, compiled for 32bit integers, can still be used for mesh
  renumbering. 

- If TFEM has been compiled with 64bit integers (option -i8 in ifort), the
  METIS-5 library needs to be compiled with 64bit integers as well. 

- The size of mesh%nodnod, which can be obtained easily as part of printinfo:

    call printinfo ( mesh, printlevel=2 )

  will output, for example

    Size of mesh%nodnod = 89328

  This number should not exceed 2^31=2147483648 (2G) when using 32bit integers.
  As an example, a cubic box with 160x160x160 27-node hexahedral elements
  (=33076161 nodes) gives a value of 2068994880=62.5*nnodes. The latter formula
  may give an estimate for general meshes as well. For tetrahedral meshes the
  factor is less than half: around 27, giving the formula 27*nnodes for the
  approximate size of mesh%nodnod.

- For problems that have a larger value than 2^31 for the size of mesh%nodnod
  METIS-5 needs to be compiled with 64bit integers.


Ad 2 (renumbering degrees):
--------------------------

A simple main program that renumbers the degrees of freedom using metis is
given by:

  program myprog

  ...

  use metis5_m

  ...

  <create and fully assemble the system matrix>

  call renumber_metis ( sysmatrix )

  ...

  end program myprog

Remarks on renumbering degrees:

- The call renumber_metis ( sysmatrix ) does not affect the internal tfem
  numbering of the degrees of freedom, since the latter has already been
  defined in the problem definition. It makes permutation arrays stored
  in the sysmatrix structure that can optionally be used by the solvers.

- Combining metis renumbering with the direct solver MA41 can lead to
  substantial speedup. It is sufficient to call renumber_metis ( sysmatrix )
  and set the solver option

    solver_options%pivot_order=1

  It also works with the version from HSL2002. Note, METIS-5 does not work
  with MA57 from the HSL library. A modified version is needed.

- The preconditioners for the iterative solvers (sparskit2) cannot
  use the renumbering directly and require column and row permutation of the
  matrix. The latter is off by default and needs to be set with the solver
  options:

    solver_options%use_renumber=.true.

  in order to use metis renumbering.

- Obviously the permutation arrays are lost if the sysmatrix has been deleted.

- The routine METIS_NodeND is used.

- For big 3D flow problems where the number of non-zeros in the matrix and/or
  preconditioner exceeds 2^31, METIS needs to be compiled with 64bit integers.

- It seems that renumbering degrees doesn't work with setting any of the
  components of the matrix input_probdef%physqmask to .false.. Metis seems to
  take forever to finish. It is unclear why this is and needs further
  investigation. The node numbering with metis is fine with any physqmask set
  to .false..
